error[SCXML052]: `<send>` to the SCXML event processor names no event
 --> tests/ui/scxml052-send-without-event.scxml:2:27
  |
2 |   <state id="a"><onentry><send target="#_internal"/></onentry><transition event="go" target="f"/></state><final id="f"/>
  |                           ^^^^ neither `event` nor `eventexpr` is present
  |
  = note: the SCXML Event I/O Processor delivers a named event, so a `<send>` it handles must have `event` or `eventexpr`; without them the send raises `error.execution` instead of delivering anything
  = help: add `event="name"` with the event to deliver, or `eventexpr` to compute it
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §6.2 <send>
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §C.1 SCXML Event I/O Processor
help: add the `event` to deliver
